  "reportMarkdown": "## Baseline Measurement Finished\n\n**Index:** 1\n**Checkpoint:** 6f40243\n**Result Commit:** none (measurement only)\n**Attempt Count:** 1\n\n### Report\n\n**Passed Status**: true — all 36 criterion bench points captured in release mode; no source edited.\n\n### Measurements (median)\n\n| Bench | Median |\n| --- | ---: |\n| delivery-queue-fanout/enqueue/1 · 32 · 256 | 341 ns · 2.81 µs · 23.8 µs |\n| signal-and-computed/signal/1 · 32 · 256 | 491 ns · 5.67 µs · 45.4 µs |\n| signal-and-computed/computed/1 · 32 · 256 | 859 ns · 6.58 µs · 52.0 µs |\n| stream-operators/filter-distinct-skip/1 · 32 · 256 | 587 ns · 8.96 µs · 73.0 µs |\n| keyed-sort-large-add-batch/640 · 1280 · 10000 | 192 µs · 402 µs · 3.58 ms |\n| keyed-watch-sparse-delivery/1 · 32 · 256 | 4.01 µs · 9.98 µs · 40.7 µs |\n| list-diff-fixed-u/640 · 1280 · 10000 | 1.14 µs · 1.63 µs · 7.09 µs |\n| live-group-touched-members/640 · 1280 · 10000 | 190 µs · 379 µs · 3.13 ms |\n| sort-and-page/load/1000 · 10000 | 204 µs · 2.19 ms |\n| sort-and-page/update/1000 · 10000 | 13.9 µs · **131.8 µs** |\n| joins-load/full_join/1000 · 4000 | 609 µs · 2.49 ms |\n| joins-load/left_join_many/1000 · 4000 | 1.64 ms · 6.84 ms |\n| transform-to-tree-load/flat/1000 · 4000 | 1.02 ms · 4.23 ms |\n| transform-to-tree-load/bushy/1000 · 4000 | 1.04 ms · 4.28 ms |\n\n### Ranked Candidate Backlog\n\n1. **Measurement gap** — no steady-state per-write benches for the most common paths (signal set/get, computed chains, effects, cache update with connect/filter/transform/bind, list push/insert/remove with filter/transform/sort/bind, pipeline loads). Mechanism: add a `hot_paths` criterion bench. Measurement enablement only.\n2. **sort-and-page single update is O(n)** — 13.9 µs @1k → 132 µs @10k (linear in cache size *n*) for one row update. Inspect `cache_sorted_page_state.rs`; expected O(log n + page).\n3. **Cache filter `visible_index_for_key` is O(n)** (`cache_dynamic_filter_state_impl.rs`) — counts included keys before the source position on every update/refresh/move once any key is excluded. Mechanism: reuse the previous filtered index when the source position is unchanged, or index the visible count.\n4. **List filter `visible_index_for_source_index` is O(index)** (`list_dynamic_filter_state.rs`, `cache_dynamic_filter_state.rs`) per change.\n5. **Source edits clone every batch for the shared envelope** (`SourceCache`/`SourceList::edit_at_version`) even when no subscriber observes `preview`/`changes`: an O(batch) deep clone per edit.\n6. **`DeliveryQueue::drain` takes three locks for a single item** (claim, pop, empty-check); `enqueue` adds a fourth. Every operator's `OrderedEmitter` pays it per batch.\n7. **`Signal::values()` locks a per-subscriber startup mutex on every live change**; an atomic live fast path would drop one mutex per delivery per subscriber.\n8. **Signal commit** — `has_subscribers` lock and change clones on every write.\n9. **Cache inline transform `visible_index` O(n)** scan.\n10. **List `transform_many` child offset O(parents)** and per-change `vec!` allocation in `offset_child_changes`.\n11. **`KeyedChangeHub::publish` locks the registry on every batch** even without watches (an atomic watch count would skip it).\n12. **Tree and join loads** (~1 µs/node; left_join_many 1.7 µs/row) — need profiling before a hypothesis.\n\nAlready-simple code to keep unchanged: `KeyOrder` (O(1)/O(log n) ticketed order), `DeliveryQueue` snapshot caching, `Subscription`.\n",
  "decisionMarkdown": "### Decision\n\nBaseline recorded; no source changed. Next: experiment 2 adds the hot-path bench (measurement enablement).\n",
